# 3. CRITICAL NEWS DUPLICATION BUG — PERMANENT FIX

CURRENT PROBLEM:

The website repeatedly publishes the same news article thousands of times. New and different news articles are not appearing correctly.

This is the highest-priority bug.

Investigate the actual root cause.

Possible causes to investigate:

- Missing unique constraints
- Incorrect slug generation
- Duplicate RSS feed entries
- Repeated scheduled function execution
- Concurrent execution race conditions
- Missing source URL validation
- Incorrect title normalization
- Duplicate React rendering
- Incorrect realtime event handling
- Repeated Firebase listeners
- Incorrect database upsert logic
- Missing provider pagination
- Incorrect article IDs
- Incorrect cache invalidation
- Repeated state appending instead of replacing/updating

Implement a reliable deduplication system.

## Required Deduplication Architecture

Every article must have:

- A stable article UUID
- A canonical source URL
- A normalized headline
- A normalized source identifier
- A unique deduplication key
- A unique slug
- A publication timestamp
- A provider/source name

Generate a deterministic deduplication key using a cryptographic hash of the canonicalized source URL.

Also use normalized headline similarity as a secondary duplicate detection mechanism.

Normalization must handle:

- Hindi Unicode text
- Extra spaces
- Punctuation
- Different URL tracking parameters
- UTM parameters
- URL fragments
- Different URL variants of the same source
- Hindi and English title variations where practical

Do not use random suffixes as a duplicate prevention strategy.

## Database-Level Protection

Implement database-level uniqueness wherever compatible with the existing schema.

Use safe, idempotent migrations.

Create appropriate unique indexes for:

- Canonical source URL
- Deduplication key
- Slug

Handle existing duplicate records safely before adding unique constraints.

Do not delete existing legitimate articles automatically.

If old duplicate records exist, create a safe deduplication migration or an admin review mechanism. Preserve the oldest legitimate record and its useful metadata.

Use atomic insert/upsert operations.

When a duplicate is found:

- Do not publish another copy.
- Do not create another article ID.
- Do not create another slug.
- Record it in automation logs.
- Continue processing other unique articles.

A duplicate article must never appear repeatedly in the public news feed.

